# pcm-notes: upstream tests (tests/parity/upstream_pcm_notes_*/) that tests/flows/test_upstream.py
# does not run against the ported flow, one per line: <test id>  <why>. Every other test of the
# app's own suite runs unchanged against store_release/flows/pcm_notes/.
test_ios_release.CatalogTests.test_catalog_drift_is_caught  reads the app's committed store files or source (listing, screenshots, catalog against the app); the app's Store checks run these through `ios pr-checks` / `catalog check`
test_ios_release.CatalogTests.test_catalog_matches_the_app_and_storekit_configuration  reads the app's committed store files or source (listing, screenshots, catalog against the app); the app's Store checks run these through `ios pr-checks` / `catalog check`
test_ios_release.CreativeGateTests.test_every_ios_switch_is_printed_and_documented  reads the app's store/gates.env.example, which store-release's own gates.env.example and docs/switches.md replace (tests/workflows/test_docs.py)
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_every_value_print_gates_accepts_is_accepted_by_the_release  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_invalid_values_are_shown_as_invalid  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
